## Failing cases at HEAD, by name

- `home en 390 px` and `home th 390 px`: `workbook-tablet-cutaway-800.webp` renders 356 x 200 and is
  40 percent covered (max 30). The dark card of the mastery graph covers the bottom-left corner. The
  photo passes at 980, 1024, and 1280 px. The spec evidence line said 60 percent at 390 px and
  76 percent at 980 px; this run reads 40 percent at 390 px and no failure above 390 px. The spec
  now records the Red numbers.
- `/products` photo cases at 390, 980, 1024, and 1280 px, en and th (8 cases):
  `blended-learning.png` is 100 percent covered. The box "See How We Report Results" and its gradient
  overlay sit on top of the file at every width.
- `/products` block cases at 390, 980, and 1280 px, en and th (6 cases): the Tutor section shows no
  photo. Only the tutor logo (SVG) sits there.
- `/products` block cases at 1024 px, en and th (2 cases): the Tutor section shows no photo, and the
  three portrait program cards render 160 x 256 against a natural 480 x 651:
  `primary-origins-2-cover.webp` (deviation 15.2 percent), `reading-origins-2-cover.webp`
  (15.2 percent), and `tutor-flashcard.webp` (22.2 percent). Tailwind `max-width: 100%` shrinks the
  width while `h-64` holds the height.

## Checks that pass, and why

- `/services/blended-learning` passes at the four widths. Its hero is a HeroSection floating image
  with no overlay. The covered instance of the same file is the `/products` card, and that case fails.
- `/products/managed-service`, `/pricing`, and `/about` pass: each hero floating image shows with no
  overlay.
- The program-card coverage cases pass at 390, 980, and 1280 px. The aspect case is what catches the
  1024 px squeeze.

## Deviations and limits

- The e2e pre-fix run at `8193625ca^` was skipped to keep the run cost down. The hero unit test proves
  the hidden-container regression there. The missing product pictures are proven at HEAD by the Tutor
  case. At `8193625ca^` the program cards carry no `data-testid` and no picture, so the same case
  fails there by construction (checked by reading the file at that commit).
- Red commits `4c48a8b12` and `5f197fd99` sit on `www/products-a62`. Nothing was pushed.
  The working tree is clean after the second commit.

